model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Creating a pool commits its app, token, account link, record and one provisioning job in a single transaction, and answers from that commit alone: no call to the pool Worker can fail a pool that is already saved. The job is a member job named after the pool's app; it sends the pool's audience through the access hook, reads that audience when it runs so a later sharing change is included, and never runs member setup. The creating request runs the job once beside its durable runner, bounded like the team installation it follows, so a pool Worker that answers has the audience before the request does. A refused, unanswered or slow attempt leaves the job queued, and the provisioning queue retries it on its own schedule and attempt limit; after the last attempt it is failed like any other job, and a repeat of the same creation request, which returns the saved pool and queues nothing new, runs it again. Recovery of a missing pool account link does not count the job, waiting or failed, as that owner's setup job. Before delivery the pool Worker admits only the owner named in the pool's own token; a new pool is private, so no one is waiting for a revocation."
    }
  }
}
